-- title:
--   Positive multiples of the axis lie in the cone
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space, let $v \in E$ be a unit vector, and let $\vartheta$ satisfy $0 < \vartheta \le \pi/2$. Write
--   $$\tilde V(v,\vartheta) \;=\; \{\,h \ne 0 : \langle v,h\rangle/\|h\| > \cos\vartheta\,\}$$
--   for the cone with axis $v$ and apex angle $\vartheta$. Then for every real $t > 0$,
--   $$t\,v \;\in\; \tilde V(v,\vartheta).$$
--
--   The axis ray is contained in its own cone: the cone is nonempty and is anchored along the direction $v$. The positivity of $\vartheta$ is what the statement needs — the defining inequality at $h = tv$ reads $\cos\vartheta < 1$ — while $t > 0$ selects the correct one of the two rays, the negative ray belonging to the opposite cone.
